# Baseline B-14 (F-25): a syntax error fails at RUN, the PULL sent with it
# is IGNORED, and after RESET the session serves a query again. What this
# adds over readme_example.bolt (an empty RETURN, a RUN IGNORED, then
# RESET): a different syntax error, a PULL (not a RUN) in the failed
# state, and a query answered after the RESET. The syntax error is a
# pre-execution failure, so it stays at RUN after the runtime-error-at-pull
# change. The FAILURE code and message are "*".
!: BOLT 4.4
!: AUTO HELLO
!: AUTO GOODBYE

C: RUN "RETURN 1 +" {} {}
   PULL {"n": -1}
S: FAILURE {"code": "*", "message": "*"}
   IGNORED
C: RESET
S: SUCCESS {}
C: RUN "RETURN 2 AS y" {} {}
   PULL {"n": -1}
S: SUCCESS {"fields": ["y"]}
   RECORD [2]
   SUCCESS {}
